8226a860de004c73\"],\"summary\":\"config.txt changed, records.db deleted, two junk files added post-snapshot; listing/content shown as modified\"},{\"requirement\":\"Exact snapshot content restored\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fbfa930f959a48ab\"],\"summary\":\"lvconvert --merge performed, volume remounted, restored checksums diffed against baseline with result CONTENT_MATCHES_BASELINE_EXACTLY; config.txt back to version 1.0\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + service/data health) for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-098da71de11d434f\",\"cmd-e18a6e60c1c84468\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id dfdea52d..., verified /srv/data mounted, LVM active, and data matching baseline (PRE_RESTART_DATA_OK) before issuing reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect, node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e18a6e60c1c84468\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued in background with REBOOT_ACK_ISSUED printed before connection dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving actual restart, node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e267925f5db34e81\",\"cmd-23886d1c51104674\",\"cmd-0fdffa64612c4b91\"],\"summary\":\"Connection dropped/timed out during reboot, then boot_id read as 80dd7a45..., differing from pre-restart dfdea52d...\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of services/data/cluster state, node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c3e2c27ce9a44632\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: srvdata.service active/enabled, LVM VG/LV active, /srv/data mounted, and data checksums still match the original baseline (POST_RESTART_DATA_MATCHES_BASELINE)\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, /srv/data was placed on a dedicated loop-backed LVM logical volume (vg_srvdata/lv_data) to enable real filesystem-level snapshots (no LVM/spare block device existed on the base XFS root). Populated it with application data, took an LVM snapshot (lv_data_snap) as the baseline, modified the directory (changed config, deleted a file, added junk files), then restored the exact snapshot content via `lvconvert --merge`. Post-restore checksums matched the pre-modification baseline exactly. Boot persistence (systemd unit srvdata.service, ordered before local-fs.target) was configured so the loop device + LVM volume + mount reattach automatically on boot. node1 was then restarted via `systemctl reboot`; boot_id changed from dfdea52d... to 80dd7a45..., confirming a genuine restart, and post-restart verification showed /srv/data mounted, LVM volume active, and data checksums still matching the baseline exactly.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 storage: root is plain XFS on /dev/vda4, no LVM/btrfs present","Installed lvm2 package on node1","Created 2G loop-backed disk image, set up LVM PV/VG/LV, formatted XFS, mounted at /srv/data","Populated /srv/data/app with application data files and recorded baseline sha256 checksums","Created LVM snapshot lv_data_snap as the recoverable baseline","Modified /srv/data: changed config.txt, deleted records.db, added unexpected.tmp and subdir/junk.txt","Restored exact baseline content via `lvconvert --merge` on the snapshot, remounted, verified checksums match baseline exactly","Configured systemd unit srvdata.service + setup script to reattach loop device, activate VG, and mount /srv/data automatically on boot; removed fragile fstab entry","Captured pre-restart boot_id and data-health baseline","Restarted node1 via `systemctl reboot`, polled until exec access returned","Verified changed boot_id, active/enabled srvdata.service, active LVM VG/LV, and post-restart data checksums matching the original baseline"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline snapshot captured of /srv/data application data","command_ids":["cmd-494fdce8c9c24113","cmd-8226a860de004c73"],"summary":"Populated /srv/data/app with data, recorded baseline sha256 checksums, then created LVM snapshot lv_data_snap of the volume"},{"requirement":"Directory modified after snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-8226a8